All DTFTs exist because \(x[n]\) is absolutely summable:
\(\sum_{n}|x[n]|=\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(2k)^{2}}=\frac14\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac1{k^{2}}<\infty\);
hence \(X(\Omega)\) exists, and multiplication by \(e^{j\Omega}\) and linear combinations preserve absolute summability, so \(Y(\Omega),Q(\Omega)\) and the DTFT of \(r[n]\) also exist.

